              "aggregatedOutput": "# Conversation dataset work\n\nWhen recording development conversations or preparing their annotations in this workspace, follow [the recording and annotation workflow](conversation-review/recording-workflow.md).\n\n- Start a separate original conversation for every new feature; keep fixes for that feature in the same conversation.\n- The new Mahjong project requires 10 features across 10 original conversations. Features 3, 4, and 5 are authorized, strictly sequentially: implement and verify feature 3 in D3 before opening D4, then implement and verify feature 4 before opening D5. Features 6–9 have been implemented and verified in their own D6–D9 conversations. Feature 10 has now been implemented and checked in D10. All ten original conversations and the 100-question package are ready for review; keep any further Feature 10 fixes within D10. Keep review approval pending.\n- Preserve actual message times and original conversation boundaries. D1, D2, and subsequent IDs must identify separately recorded conversations.\n- Match the supplied combined JSON sample, including session dates, per-session message numbering, and multiple text category labels.\n- Compare question coverage and distribution with the guide and supplied sample, including cross-session, preference, temporal, knowledge-facts, and open-domain questions. Do not count a question quota as sufficient validation.\n- Allow time for actual reading, inspection, testing, and composing requests. Do not backdate messages or claim checks that did not happen.\n- Keep work In Progress until review approval. Review comments begin with Ready for Review and include supporting evidence and the designated reviewer when known.\n# Focus Desk development\n\nRead PROJECT.md and ../conversation-review/recording-workflow.md. Implement only the assigned feature in its original conversation. All changes and evidence belong in this directory. Other feature conversations run sequentially.\n\nUse standard browser modules and Node's built-in test runner, with no build step or external runtime dependencies. Provide a polished responsive English interface with warm off-white, ink text, muted teal and accessible form controls. Domain logic should be separate from rendering and local storage should handle invalid records and failures gracefully.\n\nEvery feature must include meaningful behavior tests, actual verification results, and a concise feature review note in evidence/. Preserve status In Progress and approval pending. Do not claim unperformed browser tests. Keep product copy and project documentation free of authorship attribution. Do not edit conversation records or remove their original content.\n{\n  \"name\": \"focus-desk\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"start\": \"node server.mjs\",\n    \"test\": \"node --test\",\n    \"check\": \"node --check server.mjs && node --check src/domain.js && node --check src/focus.js && node --check src/storage.js && node --check src/app.js && node --check tests/domain.test.js && node --check tests/focus.test.js && node --check tests/storage.test.js && node --check tests/server.test.js\"\n  }\n}\n",
